TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan"},{"id":"R6","met":"yes","where":"Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Ocean acidification is stated as causing coral bleaching. Bleaching is primarily driven by thermal stress, so the causal claim is wrong or overstated."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The claim that bleaching is displacing billions of animals is unsupported by any cited source."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The 10 m GSD requirement is not derived from the detection method in [4] (airborne imaging), so the resolution requirement is unjustified."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"The coverage argument compares 2,700 km track spacing with five passes but does not compute a revisit or repeat-cycle time, so the weekly-coverage conclusion is not quantified."},{"where":"Project Plan","issue":"Week 10 is described as having no new design work and final simulation by Week 9, but the Gantt chart and Editing text schedule STK simulations and final simulations in Week 10."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","issue":"Launch analysis required by R2 (launch vehicle, trajectory, site) is not done; only orbit calculations are presented."}],"overall":"Strong, well-structured Part 1 with a clear mission concept, user mapping, Gantt, risk table, sources and correct orbit calculations. Deductions: no launch analysis (R2), acidification causal error, unjustified 10 m GSD, Week 10 simulation inconsistency, and an incomplete coverage argument. Marks are on the 0-10 level scale.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":32.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"Mission goal, four measurable objectives and named users (AIMS, GBRMPA, CSIRO/universities, BoM) are clear, and each objective is tied to a user need, with literature cited. Weaker points: the acidification causal claim, the unjustified 10 m GSD ('to be refined'), and a thin argument for why a new satellite is needed beyond existing NOAA products.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Give reef managers direct, repeatable observations of coral colour over the whole Great Barrier Reef"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Objectives 1 and 3 come directly from the managers' need to react within days"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"Gantt chart, task descriptions, a risk table with triggers and responses, and a sourced information list give a robust, feasible plan. The task order is justified by the mission logic (orbit before ground and comms; end of life after orbit). Week 10 is inconsistent: text says no new design work and final simulation by week 9, yet the Gantt shows STK simulations in Week 10.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Final design and simulation should be completed by the end of week 9."},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Project Plan","quote":"Table 1: Project risks and contingency plans."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":8.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Hand calculations for period, sun-synchronous inclination, ground-track shift and swath are correct and checked against the STK scenario, with an interpretation that identifies the key swath-versus-resolution trade. No STK output is shown, and the coverage argument stops short of a computed revisit time, so it is not fully conclusive.","evidence":[{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 and 4 are complete."},{"where":"Preliminary Progress","quote":"Weekly coverage (objective 1) is therefore not guaranteed by one satellite at this altitude and resolution."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":8.0,"scale":10.0,"points":16.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Clear headed structure, consistent IEEE-style citations in order of appearance, and labelled figure and tables. Some sentences are awkward ('not even the full extent of their nurture'). Several references lack authors or dates ([4], [8], [9]), and [11] is a weak source, which slightly lowers consistency.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"but this is not even the full extent of their nurture"},{"where":"References","quote":"NOAA Coral Reef Watch, report on satellite monitoring of reef vulnerability."}]}]}
